    "list_source": {
      "title": "Utah cities charge transportation fees on top of taxes",
      "publisher": "KUTV",
      "url": "https://kutv.com/news/local/utah-cities-charge-transportation-fees-on-top-of-taxes",
      "published": "2026-03-25",
      "retrieved": "2026-08-03"
    },
    "caveats": [
      "The fee is flat. Every household pays the same, whatever the home is worth, so it lands hardest on the least valuable homes — the opposite of how a property tax rate works.",
      "The rate equivalents are what each fee would cost as a property tax rate on a $500,000 primary residence, taxed on 55% of value. They are for scale only; no city levies these as a rate.",
      "A fee is not a tax. It is set by resolution and is not subject to Truth-in-Taxation notices or hearings, which is part of why cities use it. Utah's Supreme Court upheld Pleasant Grove's as a fee rather than a tax in 2023, remanding on whether the amount was reasonable.",
      "About a dozen Utah cities charge one; these four are the Utah County cities identified in a March 2026 survey and confirmed against each city's current fee schedule. A city that adopted one since would not appear here."
    ]
  },
